{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793599905,"nonce":"lKTc+7BRnUgQe/iT2DY5q3MAirA=","message":"Scope and exit criterion changed after the 2026-11-01 roadmap review (design §11 and §12 updated to match).\n\nScope:\n\n- Recursion: structural only. C# recursion over `int`/`long` is never structural, and well-founded recursion needs decrease proofs that only M5's tactics can produce; WF definitions also barely reduce in the kernel, which the differential tests rely on. Well-founded recursion with `Spec.Decreases` moves to M5.\n- Theorems: only theorems without free parameters, closed by `rfl`/`decide` proof terms the translator emits directly. `decide` cannot enumerate quantified `Int32` parameters, and nothing builds proof terms before `LeanSharp.Meta`. Quantified theorems and the `Prove` syntax move to M5.\n- Rejected with a diagnostic until M6: `/`, `%`, checked arithmetic (including projects with `CheckForOverflowUnderflow`). Non-null record parameters are recorded as assumptions for the M6 assumption report. Otherwise these would be silent approximations (design §2).\n- Enums added to the subset; decide §12 Q3 (open vs `[Closed]`) here.\n- Semantics library v0 gets the §10.6 CLR-agreement tests for every modelled operation.\n\nExit criterion, replacing the old one:\n\nA fixed corpus translates, including a `Validate`-shaped method over records and enums (`int` in place of `decimal`). Differential tests pass, with generators that include zero divisors, `MinValue / -1` and null records. Theorems without free parameters are closed by translator-emitted `rfl`/`decide` proof terms. Everything admitted exports and passes `scripts/cross-check.sh`.\n\nOpen questions retimed: Q10 is pinned for now to Lean v4.33.1 / lean4export `15f6055` (the kernel's version). Decide Q13 (target framework) before M4 starts and Q12 (name) before the user API package is published.","files":null}]}